WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:06.191
Satchel packs a practice set into one HTML file. The questions and answers in this demonstration are fictional.

2
00:00:06.191 --> 00:00:12.274
Write questions in plain text. These three include a typed fraction, a multiple-choice question and a number.

3
00:00:12.274 --> 00:00:21.355
A missing answer key blocks download. Correcting the question makes the complete set available again.

4
00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:27.509
Download the actual HTML file. The recording then opens that file with network access disabled in the browser.

5
00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:33.603
This downloaded set is about 32 KB. It opens directly from a file; no account or installation is needed.

6
00:00:33.603 --> 00:00:41.765
Hints, larger text and high contrast keep the unfinished answer. Here, 5 is deliberately the wrong answer.

7
00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:51.351
Reload the same file and continue at question 1. The unfinished answer is restored in this tested Chrome browser.

8
00:00:51.351 --> 00:01:01.544
Checking shows the right answer and explanation. The other two answers are correct, including 1,000 with a grouping comma.

9
00:01:01.544 --> 00:01:09.664
The result is 2 of 3 right. Reloading preserves the completed attempt, and the missed question can be practised again.

10
00:01:09.664 --> 00:01:19.796
Save a real text report while offline. It records checked answers, explanations and hint use; the copyable view contains the same text.

11
00:01:19.796 --> 00:01:29.459
Retry only the missed question. The answer 1/2 is accepted as equivalent to .5; the retry is labelled separately.

12
00:01:29.459 --> 00:01:38.530
A report can be saved or copied for the learner to share. Nothing is handed in automatically. These are practice records, not verified grades.
